 # Changelog
 
+## 1.6.0
+
+- Ticket assignment. `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` with `{"assignee": "<agent>"}` assigns an open or in-progress ticket
+  (`{"assignee": null}` unassigns it; an agent is a name of 1 to 64 characters). The agent is notified. Assigning a ticket
+  to the agent it already has changes nothing. `GET /tickets?assignee=<agent>` lists an agent's tickets, `assignee=` the
+  unassigned ones.
+- A ticket must now match every filter of the listing, as the API always said: `?status=open&priority=urgent` listed
+  the tickets that were open or urgent.
+- `ASSIGNEES=on` shows `assignee` on every ticket; until then tickets look as they did in 1.5.0. The data file holds the
+  assignees either way, and the format is still version 1.
+- `bin/tickets.js list` shows the assignee (a column of the table, a last column of `--raw`) and takes `--assignee`.
+
 ## 1.5.0
 
 - Due times ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)). Every ticket gets a due time, `due`: the time it was created
